		  { id: "A", text: "Passengers are completely free to leave the scene immediately when the vehicle pulls over" },
		  { id: "B", text: "Passengers must drive the vehicle if the driver is arrested" },
		  { id: "C", text: "Passengers are considered 'seized' during a traffic stop along with the driver, giving them standing to challenge the stop's legality" },
		  { id: "D", text: "Passengers have automatic immunity from any contraband found in the vehicle" }
		],
		answer: "C",
		explain: "Brendlin v. California established that a passenger is seized during a traffic stop and therefore has the Fourth Amendment right to challenge the legality of that stop. [Category: Case Law]"
	},

